  "explanation": "The sources explicitly identify Alfred Cannan as a 'Turkish MP' (D1S3, D1S12) representing Istanbul's Beyoğlu district and a 'politician' (D1S3). Document 2 explicitly states he holds the position of 'Minister for the Treasury' in the Isle of Man (D2S3, D2S14). While other terms like 'Member of the Grand National Assembly of Turkey' (C3) and 'Representative of Istanbul's Beyoğlu district' (C4) are factually supported by the text, they are semantically equivalent to the accepted 'Turkish MP' and 'Politician' labels respectively, so the concise forms from R5 are preserved. Terms like 'Leader of the opposition party' (C6, C14) are incorrect as the text attributes this to a colleague named Emine. Descriptive phrases like 'Economic policy shaper' (C7) or 'Fiscal steward' (C8) describe his actions or titles in a narrative sense rather than specific official positions held, and are thus excluded in favor of the direct role titles."
